    "title": "Los Angeles Dodgers TV Schedule",
    "text": "Mark your calendars as the defending World Series champion Los Angeles Dodgers take the field for the 2026 season with the following local and national TV schedule. For the full MLB schedule, see the preceding link. If you purchase a subscription through a link on this page, this site may receive a commission. Today Time (UTC)Game / TV12:20 amCleveland Guardians vs Los Angeles DodgersMLBN, MLB.tv, MLB Extra Innings | A CleGuardians.TV | H SNLA | SN+ Friday, April 3 Time (UTC)Game / TV5:05 pmLos Angeles Dodgers vs Washington NationalsMLB.tv, MLB Extra Innings | A SNLA | H Nationals.TV Saturday, April 4 Time (UTC)Game / TV8:05 pmLos Angeles Dodgers vs Washington NationalsMLB.tv, MLB Extra Innings | A SNLA | H Nationals.TV Sunday, April 5 Time (UTC)Game / TV5:35 pmLos Angeles Dodgers vs Washington NationalsMLB.tv, MLB Extra Innings | A SNLA | H Nationals.TV Monday, April 6 Time (UTC)Game / TV11:07 pmLos Angeles Dodgers vs Toronto Blue JaysFS1, FOX One Tuesday, April 7 Time (UTC)Game / TV11:07 pmLos Angeles Dodgers vs Toronto Blue JaysTBS Wednesday, April 8 Time (UTC)Game / TV7:07 pmLos Angeles Dodgers vs Toronto Blue JaysMLB.tv, MLB Extra Innings How to stream Dodgers games in 2026 (Illustration) | Spectrum SportsNet LA Logo – Courtesy: Charter Communications, Guggenheim Baseball Management, Los Angeles Dodgers | SNLA+ Logo – Courtesy: Charter Communications, Guggenheim Baseball Management, Los Angeles Dodgers, Major League Baseball AM 570 LA Sports Logo – Courtesy: iHeartMedia, Los Angeles Dodgers Direct-to-Subscriber Platforms Local games (Spectrum SportsNet LA): SNLA+ (in-market-only): Available as a standalone subscription through MLB for $30/month or $200/season. Access to Dodgers telecasts and other programming on Spectrum SportsNet LA. MLB.TV (out-of-market only): All out-of-market locally televised games. New users purchase MLB.TV subscriptions through ESPN, which includes a one-month free trial of ESPN Unlimited that be canceled at any time. Existing subscribers to MLB.TV are auto-renewed as usual. Consumers can watch MLB.TV through the league’s platform or ESPN with valid authentication. More information about local Dodgers broadcasts can be found here. National games: Peacock: All NBC Sports-produced games on the NBC broadcast network and Peacock. ESPN Unlimited: All ESPN-produced games on the ESPN cable networks and ABC, plus the ability to purchase MLB.TV as an add-on subscription. Disney+: Occasional simulcasts of ESPN-produced games. Apple TV: All “Friday Night Baseball” games throughout the season. HBO Max: All TNT Sports-produced games on the TBS cable network. Fox One: All Fox Sports-produced games on the Fox broadcast network and FS1. Netflix: Access to watch Opening Night, the Home Run Derby and the MLB at Field of Dreams Game. Team Total ABC Apple TV ESPN Fox FS1 MLB Network NBC Netflix Peacock TBS Los Angeles Dodgers 22 0 3 1 6 2 4 4 0 0 2 Cable and Streaming Bundles YouTube TV: All games on ESPN/ABC, NBC, Fox/FS1 and TBS. Some Peacock-exclusive games will be available via NBCSN. (Peacock can also be purchased in full through YouTube Channels). Sponsored offer: Get $75 off YouTube TV ($15 off for 5 months) when you sign up today. New users only. Cancel Anytime. Terms apply. Sling: All games on ESPN/ABC (ABC games will be on ESPN3), Fox/FS1, NBC and TBS. Fubo: All games on ESPN/ABC and Fox/FS1. DIRECTV (stream): All games on ESPN/ABC, NBC, Fox/FS1 and TBS. Linear cable (ex. Dish Network, Xfinity, DIRECTV): All games on ESPN/ABC, NBC, Fox/FS1 and TBS. Hulu + Live TV: All games on ESPN/ABC, NBC, Fox/FS1 and TBS. In-Person See the Dodgers in person at Dodger Stadium, or catch Major League Baseball games from any of the 30 ballparks this season, by purchasing tickets through Vivid Seats, SeatGeek or Gametime.",
